WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.750 --> 00:00:04.420
There are countless reasons to get hyped up
for Spider-Man: Far From Home there's the

00:00:04.420 --> 00:00:08.580
web-slinging action, the international setting,
and getting to see what comes next in the

00:00:08.580 --> 00:00:10.260
MCU after Avengers: Endgame.

00:00:10.460 --> 00:00:13.820
But if you think that the excitement stops
when the final shot of Far From Home fades

00:00:13.820 --> 00:00:15.400
to black, you're sorely mistaken.

00:00:15.540 --> 00:00:19.460
We can confirm that there's a surprise cameo
included in a mid-credits scene that will

00:00:19.460 --> 00:00:22.260
make longtime Spider-Man fans totally freak
out.

00:00:22.270 --> 00:00:25.840
It goes without saying that we're going to
get into major spoilers for Spider-Man: Far

00:00:25.840 --> 00:00:27.140
From Home from this point on.

00:00:27.320 --> 00:00:31.300
Those hoping to walk into theaters with a
clear head and no context, turn away.

00:00:31.300 --> 00:00:34.140
Everyone else, stick with us as we reveal
the epic cameo.

00:00:34.780 --> 00:00:38.780
The mid-credits scene takes Peter and MJ back
to New York City, where a news report plays

00:00:38.780 --> 00:00:41.240
out on a huge screen to a crowd of bystanders.

00:00:41.460 --> 00:00:45.030
It's up on that screen that fans will see
a familiar face: none other than The Daily

00:00:45.030 --> 00:00:47.120
Bugle founder J. Jonah Jameson.

00:00:47.350 --> 00:00:51.160
What's even better about this cameo is that
it isn't just any actor playing Jameson in

00:00:51.170 --> 00:00:53.110
the Spider-Man: Far From Home mid-credits
scene.

00:00:53.110 --> 00:00:57.220
It's J.K. Simmons, who famously portrayed
the crazed newsman in director Sam Raimi's

00:00:57.220 --> 00:00:59.860
original Spider-Man film trilogy from the
2000s.

00:00:59.940 --> 00:01:05.640
Simmons last sported Jameson's signature toothbrush
mustache and flattop haircut in 2007's Spider-Man

00:01:05.659 --> 00:01:09.939
3, meaning his cameo appearance in Far From
Home is the first time in over a decade that

00:01:09.940 --> 00:01:12.140
he's assumed the role for a live-action project.

00:01:12.280 --> 00:01:16.720
In true Jameson fashion, the Daily Bugle blowhard
is in a huge huff over Spider-Man's antics

00:01:16.720 --> 00:01:18.440
in the Far From Home mid-credits scene.

00:01:18.740 --> 00:01:23.740
The news report includes an exclusive clip
originally released by the "controversial

00:01:23.740 --> 00:01:27.500
news website" TheDailyBugle.net, which shows
Peter giving orders to quote "execute them

00:01:27.500 --> 00:01:28.000
all."

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:31.540
This is obviously doctored, as we know Spider-Man
would never do such a thing.

00:01:31.600 --> 00:01:35.820
Still, many New Yorkers take it at face value,
believing that the formerly-friendly neighborhood

00:01:35.820 --> 00:01:38.200
hero was the one who orchestrated the attack
on London.

00:01:38.720 --> 00:01:43.120
The events of Spider-Man: Far From Home reveal
the actual perpetrator and it definitely isn't

00:01:43.120 --> 00:01:43.620
Spidey.

00:01:43.620 --> 00:01:47.540
Jameson pushes a contrasting narrative: that
Spider-Man is a menace, and the villain of

00:01:47.549 --> 00:01:49.250
Far From Home is really a hero.

00:01:49.250 --> 00:01:50.600
"Who is Spider-Man?

00:01:51.100 --> 00:01:52.380
He's a criminal!  That's who he is.

00:01:53.160 --> 00:01:53.840
A vigilante!

00:01:54.240 --> 00:01:55.160
A public menace!

00:01:55.540 --> 00:01:56.880
What's he doing on my front page?"

00:01:56.980 --> 00:02:01.020
Many fans speculated that Spider-Man: Far
From Home would include a cameo from J. Jonah

00:02:01.020 --> 00:02:05.140
Jameson, with some outlets even running early
reports that it was definitely true.

00:02:05.300 --> 00:02:08.700
Though it was difficult to prove the claims
at that time, we can now say with certainty

00:02:08.700 --> 00:02:09.560
that they were accurate.

00:02:09.560 --> 00:02:13.760
Even without any leaks and rumors and theories,
there was a big piece of evidence to suggest

00:02:13.760 --> 00:02:18.480
a J. Jonah Jameson cameo in Spider-Man: Far
From Home: Simmons' attendance at the film's

00:02:18.480 --> 00:02:21.080
world premiere in Hollywood on Wednesday,
June 26.

00:02:21.430 --> 00:02:25.040
Considering Simmons wasn't on the red carpet
for the premiere of Spider-Man: Homecoming

00:02:25.040 --> 00:02:29.110
because he wasn't in that movie, Marvel super
fans began putting two and two together: Simmons'

00:02:29.110 --> 00:02:31.980
Jameson would probably be in Far From Home
in some capacity.

00:02:32.320 --> 00:02:33.520
Turns out that they were right.

00:02:33.860 --> 00:02:38.000
Though the J. Jonah Jameson cameo in Far From
Home is sure to make audiences scream and

00:02:38.010 --> 00:02:41.000
shout in their seats, it's only the start
of the after-credits fun.

00:02:41.000 --> 00:02:45.130
Far From Home also includes a post-credits
scene that confirms a popular theory fans

00:02:45.130 --> 00:02:46.380
have discussed for months on end.

00:02:46.380 --> 00:02:50.300
We won't spoil it for you here, but anyone
who has seen Captain Marvel and speculated

00:02:50.300 --> 00:02:53.930
that a certain element from that superhero
flick might pop up in Far From Home will go

00:02:53.930 --> 00:02:55.960
nuts over the film's post-credits stinger.

00:02:56.150 --> 00:03:00.440
Look forward to seeing J. Jonah Jameson in
Spider-Man: Far From Home when the film swings

00:03:00.460 --> 00:03:02.080
into theaters on July 2.

